course: dictionary
lesson: 1337
title: Words from other languages
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words in English come from other languages, and you may meet them in books. «Camion» is one of them. It is rare in English, so you may not know it. Use the context clues to work out its meaning.
explain: In old military history texts, a camion is a low, strong truck or cart that carries heavy things. If a text says soldiers loaded heavy crates onto a camion, the clues show it is a big, strong vehicle for carrying loads.
explain: The same word can mean different things in different languages. In French, «un camion» is a lorry. In Spanish, «un camión» is a truck. Swap the meaning into the sentence to check that it still makes sense.
explain: Look at the French example: «rouge means red and already ends in e: une pomme rouge, un camion rouge.» The word rouge stays the same with both words because it already ends in e. Clues like this help you learn how words work together.
fact: Camion is a noun. You can write a camion or camions.
fact: In English, camion is rare, and you mostly meet it in old military history texts.
fact: A camion is a low, strong truck or cart used to carry heavy things, especially in the army.
fact: In French, «un camion» means a lorry or truck.
fact: In Spanish, «camión» means a truck, and in Mexico it can also mean a bus. French says it ka-mee-ON, with a nasal end.
exercise: «The soldiers loaded heavy crates onto the camion.» What is a camion? | A small bird that sings at dawn | *A low, strong truck or cart for heavy things | A type of silver coin | A soft cushion for a chair
exercise: In French, what does «un camion» mean? | A river boat | A bicycle | *A lorry | A small cake
exercise: Why does rouge stay the same in «une pomme rouge» and «un camion rouge»? | *Because rouge already ends in e | Because rouge means blue | Because rouge is a longer word | Because pomme and camion both mean red
test: «The camion rumbled slowly across the old bridge, loaded with sacks of grain.» What is a camion most like? | A tiny bird | *A heavy truck | A pair of shoes | A kind of flower
test: In Mexico, what can «camión» mean in Spanish, besides a truck? | A train | A bicycle | A boat | *A bus
exam: How does French say camion? | *ka-mee-ON, with a nasal end | ka-mee-OT | cam-ee-ON, with a hard c | KAM-ee-un
